{"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/UIKitTracking\/documentation\/UIKitTracking"},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/uikittracking"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"kind":"symbol","sections":[],"metadata":{"role":"collection","roleHeading":"Framework","modules":[{"name":"UIKitTracking"}],"title":"UIKitTracking","externalID":"UIKitTracking","symbolKind":"module"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Use this module to track events from UIKit views, view controllers and controls on iOS, iPadOS,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"tvOS, visionOS and Mac Catalyst; elsewhere it builds empty, and on macOS and watchOS its API isn’t"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"there. SwiftUI views use"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/swiftuitracking","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and AppKit views on macOS use"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/appkittracking","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The tracker is a UIKit trait, ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TrackerTrait"},{"text":". Set it on a window scene’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"traitOverrides"},{"text":" as the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"scene connects, and every view controller and view in the scene’s windows inherits it, the way","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"SwiftUI views inherit their environment. Read it in any of them as ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"traitCollection.tracker"},{"text":". A","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"view controller or view can set its own for everything below it, and each scene keeps its own, so","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"two windows can track through two trackers. Until a tracker is set, the trait holds","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Tracker.noOp"},{"text":", which drops every event.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"UIControl.track(_:for:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" tracks an event each time a control sends the given control events","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"code":".primaryActionTriggered","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" by default), through the tracker the control’s traits hold at that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"moment:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["import Traffluent","import UIKit","","@Event","struct ShareTapped {}","","@Event","struct CheckoutStarted {","    var cartSize: Int","}","","final class CartViewController: UIViewController {","    let share = UIButton(configuration: .filled())","    let checkOut = UIButton(configuration: .filled())","","    override func viewDidLoad() {","        super.viewDidLoad()","        share.track(ShareTapped())  \/\/ through the tracker the button's traits hold when it is tapped","        checkOut.addTarget(self, action: #selector(checkOut(_:)), for: .primaryActionTriggered)","        view.addSubview(share)","        view.addSubview(checkOut)","    }","","    @objc func checkOut(_ sender: UIButton) {","        sender.traitCollection.tracker.track(CheckoutStarted(cartSize: 3))","    }","}","","\/\/ In the scene delegate's scene(_:willConnectTo:options:):","windowScene.traitOverrides.tracker = tracker"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"track(_:for:)"},{"text":" adds a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UIAction"},{"text":" beside the control’s other actions and targets, so they still","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"run, and returns it; pass it to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"removeAction(_:for:)"},{"text":" to stop tracking. Where SwiftUI hosts","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"UIKit, or UIKit hosts SwiftUI, the trait and SwiftUI’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\\.tracker"},{"text":" are one value.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The guide","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/trackingfromviews","type":"reference"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"covers all three frameworks.","type":"text"}]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"API","text":"API"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The documentation site is built on Linux, where the module is empty, so its symbols have no pages","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of their own here. Their doc comments are in the sources, and Xcode shows them for an iOS target.","type":"text"}]},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"TrackerTrait","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":": the trait holding the tracker, "},{"code":"Tracker.noOp","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" until one is set."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UITraitCollection.tracker"},{"type":"text","text":": reads the trait."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"UIMutableTraits.tracker","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":": sets the trait on a window scene’s, view controller’s or view’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"traitOverrides","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"UIControl.track(_:for:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":": tracks an event each time the control sends the given control events."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"}]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Hand UIKit views and view controllers their tracker as a trait, and track what controls do."}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"references":{"https://tyler-keith-thompson.github.io/Traffluent/documentation/swiftuitracking":{"type":"link","title":"SwiftUITracking","url":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/swiftuitracking","identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/swiftuitracking","titleInlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiftUITracking"}]},"https://tyler-keith-thompson.github.io/Traffluent/documentation/appkittracking":{"titleInlineContent":[{"code":"AppKitTracking","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"link","title":"AppKitTracking","url":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/appkittracking","identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/appkittracking"},"https://tyler-keith-thompson.github.io/Traffluent/documentation/traffluent/trackingfromviews":{"titleInlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Tracking from SwiftUI, UIKit and AppKit"}],"url":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/trackingfromviews","identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/trackingfromviews","title":"Tracking from SwiftUI, UIKit and AppKit","type":"link"},"doc://UIKitTracking/documentation/UIKitTracking":{"type":"topic","title":"UIKitTracking","url":"\/documentation\/uikittracking","identifier":"doc:\/\/UIKitTracking\/documentation\/UIKitTracking","role":"collection","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Hand UIKit views and view controllers their tracker as a trait, and track what controls do.","type":"text"}]}}}